From cb7960c8a6e0ac5f446e80d4afcf2dca2bbf0d24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "William Mark Katzenmeyer, P.E., C.F.M." <heccommander@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:12:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] hdf5-reader: checked arithmetic for file-derived index
 and heap sizes

[L13] Status vs upstream v0.9.3: NOT UPSTREAM (PR #100 fixed other sites only).
Kind: safety fix. Proposed upstream grouping: PR-B hardening.
Applies on roteiro-gis/netcdf-rust v0.9.3 (3d708fd) after the earlier patches of this series.

Fixed array: compute data block geometry (paged length in closed form,
page sizes, entry offsets) with checked arithmetic, require the whole
block before sizing the entry vector, range-check entry indices and
reject zero chunk dimensions. Previously a wrapped nelmts * entry_size led
to a 1.7 EB Vec::with_capacity and the paged length loop could run 2^61
iterations.

Extensible array: saturating super block layout, checked entry offsets,
entry runs sized from the remaining bytes, and placeholder entries capped
at the dataset's chunk count.

Also check the global heap collection end and padding, object header
chunk and continuation ranges (minimum continuation length, checksum
slices via get()), and nbit/scale-offset output offsets.
